 "Casey at the Bat."

1067
00:42:11,900 --> 00:42:14,460
-[SCREAMS]

1068
00:42:14,460 --> 00:42:16,530
-She must have studied
 under Jamie Lee Curtis.

1069
00:42:19,490 --> 00:42:24,920
-[SCREAMS]

1070
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:26,060
-Eh, hang on.

1071
00:42:26,060 --> 00:42:26,780
Oh, my ankle.

1072
00:42:26,780 --> 00:42:27,280
Ow.

1073
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:29,120
-[SCREAMS]

1074
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:31,670
-"Grady," this fall on NBC.

1075
00:42:31,670 --> 00:42:32,170
-Hey, Fred.

1076
00:42:32,170 --> 00:42:32,670
-Look at that.

1077
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:42,490
-She's briskly jogging from him.

1078
00:42:42,490 --> 00:42:44,000
-You know, he did kill
 that creep for her.

1079
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,990
She could thank him, at least.

1080
00:42:46,990 --> 00:42:51,900
-Hey, it's your typical
 free week at the Y.

1081
00:42:51,900 --> 00:42:54,740
-Hey, come on back and
 shag some flies for me.

1082
00:42:57,720 --> 00:43:00,560
-Don't use the exit.

1083
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:02,930
-Come on, we need a
 short center fielder.

1084
00:43:06,540 --> 00:43:07,740
-Oh, zombie never
 could hit a curve.

1085
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,820
-You know, John Goodman
 on Hume Cronin's back

1086
00:43:12,820 --> 00:43:14,130
could outrun this guy.

1087
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:20,150
-Oh, no, her bra strap broke.

1088
00:43:20,150 --> 00:43:20,920
-What next?

1089
00:43:20,920 --> 00:43:22,600
-[SCREAMS]

1090
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,890
-OK, OK, I'm giving
 you a head start.

1091
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:30,130
-(SINGING) Woke up,
 fell out of bed,

1092
00:43:30,130 --> 00:43:32,350
dragged the comb across my head.

1093
00:43:32,350 --> 00:43:33,680
-(SINGING) Found my
 way down the stairs.

1094
00:43:33,680 --> 00:43:34,480
-What's going to happen?

1095
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,050
I-- oh.

1096
00:43:47,490 --> 00:43:51,530
-(SINGING) Touchdown in the
 land of the Delta blues,

1097
00:43:51,530 --> 00:43:57,830
in the middle of
 the pouring rain.

1098
00:43:57,830 --> 00:43:59,260
-Oh, wonderful.

1099
00:43:59,260 --> 00:44:00,210
-Yeah.

1100
00:44:00,210 --> 00:44:01,590
-Hey, thanks for that back rub.

1101
00:44:01,590 --> 00:44:03,470
-Water feels great.

1102
00:44:03,470 --> 00:44:05,580
-Yeah, hardly feel
 those injuries

1103
00:44:05,580 --> 00:44:07,100
I sustained when
 you ran me over.

1104
00:44:07,100 --> 00:44:11,280
-[LAUGHS] Let me just
 say, I am totally relaxed.

1105
00:44:11,280 --> 00:44:14,330
-[GIGGLES] Servo,
 stop that! [GIGGLES]

1106
00:44:14,330 --> 00:44:15,280
-What?
 What, Crow?

1107
00:44:15,280 --> 00:44:15,820
What?
 Huh?

1108
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:16,320
What?

1109
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,250
-Stop it, you nutty nut nut.

1110
00:44:17,250 --> 00:44:18,940
-Crow, I'm not doing anything.

1111
00:44:18,940 --> 00:44:21,170
[SCREAMING]

1112
00:44:21,170 --> 00:44:22,080
[SPITTING]

1113
00:44:22,080 --> 00:44:22,980
-Hey, guys.

1114
00:44:22,980 --> 00:44:24,040
[SCREAMING]

1115
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:24,540
-Dinner?

1116
00:44:24,540 --> 00:44:26,150
[SCREAMING]

1117
00:44:26,150 --> 00:44:27,240
[ALARM]

1118
00:44:41,660 --> 00:44:42,640
-Where'd you get the fish?

1119
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:44,110
-I got it--

1120
00:44:44,110 --> 00:44:46,290
-Hey, Conan O'Brien.

1121
00:44:46,290 --> 00:44:49,120
-We didn't do it.

1122
00:44:49,120 --> 00:44:51,400
-Another unruly crowd.

1123
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:52,120
-Frank.

1124
00:44:52,120 --> 00:44:52,880
-Yeah?

1125
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:54,180
Forensic's just about finished.

1126
00:44:54,180 --> 00:44:55,610
The ME wants to see you inside.

1127
00:44:55,610 --> 00:44:58,650
-What did I do?

1128
00:44:58,650 --> 00:44:59,420
-Great.

1129
00:44:59,420 --> 00:45:02,760
-Fine, everybody dump on me.

1130
00:45:02,760 --> 00:45:07,830
-Look, uh, keep an eye on
 my star witness here, OK?

1131
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,690
-Say, officer, can I go now?

1132
00:45:09,690 --> 00:45:10,800
-Uh, soon.

1133
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:12,440
I've got a few more questions.

1134
00:45:12,440 --> 00:45:15,130
-Can I have a Tahitian treat?

1135
00:45:15,130 --> 00:45:16,110
-Poor guy.

1136
00:45:18,670 --> 00:45:21,420
-Hmm.

1137
00:45:21,420 --> 00:45:22,970
Yep, yep, this is
 the scene they always

1138
00:45:22,970 --> 00:45:25,120
show on "That's Hollywood,"
 with Tom Bosley.

1139
00:45:25,120 --> 00:45:25,620
-Beautiful.

1140
00:45:25,620 --> 00:45:26,850
Beautiful.

1141
00:45:26,850 --> 00:45:28,850
-That's Bosley.

1142
00:45:28,850 --> 00:45:30,890
-Now let's get one
 of you with the body.

1143
00:45:30,890 --> 00:45:32,670
-Wishful thinking, doc?

1144
00:45:32,670 --> 00:45:34,230
-Ah, Frank.

1145
00:45:34,230 --> 00:45:36,940
Nice to see you could
 make it to the clambake.

1146
00:45:36,940 --> 00:45:39,150
-Are you talking to the Penguin?

1147
00:45:39,150 --> 00:45:40,680
-Oh, what the hell Else?
 would I be doing at 3

1148
00:45:40,680 --> 00:45:41,620
o'clock in the morning?

1149
00:45:41,620 --> 00:45:42,440
-I don't want to know.

1150
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:44,910
-See your boys in white
 are moving right along.

1151
00:45:44,910 --> 00:45:49,040
-Well, you've probably noticed
 the lovely lady on her way out.

1152
00:45:49,040 --> 00:45:51,460
-Now the boys are
 trying to fish lover-boy

1153
00:45:51,460 --> 00:45:53,530
out of the swimming
 pool full of blood.

1154
00:45:53,530 --> 00:45:55,360
-Uh, about your voice.

1155
00:45:55,360 --> 00:45:57,400
-You get anything out
 of the good old Joe?

1156
00:45:57,400 --> 00:46:00,430
-Oh, old Joe is a wealth
 of useful information.

1157
00:46:00,430 --> 00:46:00,930
-Yeah?

1158
00:46:00,930 --> 00:46:04,470
-Do you know how many times they
 refinish the floors in here?

1159
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:05,900
-[LAUGHS]

1160
00:46:05,900 --> 00:46:06,840
-[LAUGHS]

1161
00:46:06,840 --> 00:46:10,130
-According to Joe, nobody
 came in, no one could get in.

1162
00:46:10,130 --> 00:46:14,360
Now, bodies A and B stayed late
 for a post-game celebration,

1163
00:46:14,360 --> 00:46:15,200
as was their habit.

1164
00:46:15,200 --> 00:46:18,410
Old Joe was sleeping like a
 baby, never heard a thing.

1165
00:46:18,410 --> 00:46:20,340
-So who put the 12-year-old
 in charge of the investigation

1166
00:46:20,340 --> 00:46:21,990
here?

1167
00:46:21,990 --> 00:46:24,390
-So what do you
 think, double suicide?

1168
00:46:24,390 --> 00:46:25,140
-No thanks.

1169
00:46:25,140 --> 00:46:26,960
-Oh, sure, sure.

1170
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:31,630
Lover-boy smashes her head
 in with the baseball bat,

1171
00:46:31,630 --> 00:46:35,990
then snaps his own neck
 with his bare hands

1172
00:46:35,990 --> 00:46:38,790
and throws himself in
 the pool out of remorse.

1173
00:46:38,790 --> 00:46:40,480
-Well, you're the tailor.

1174
00:46:40,480 --> 00:46:41,950
-Bare hands?

1175
00:46:41,950 --> 00:46:43,520
From the looks of it, yeah.

1176
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:45,600
-Boy, police work
 is really hard.

1177
00:46:45,600 --> 00:46:47,980
-So unless old Joe is
 secretly pumping iron--

1178
00:46:47,980 --> 00:46:53,600
-You're looking for one
 large, angry person.

1179
00:46:53,600 --> 00:46:55,650
-Maybe I am looking
 for someone like that,

1180
00:46:55,650 --> 00:46:57,720
but I don't think
 I'll ever find him.

1181
00:47:03,730 --> 00:47:04,980
-Don't touch me.

1182
00:47:04,980 --> 00:47:08,290
-I guess I'll need more
 tape than I thought.

1183
00:47:08,290 --> 00:47:09,690
[MUSIC BLARING]

1184
00:47:09,690 --> 00:47:11,920
-Geez.

1185
00:47:11,920 --> 00:47:16,010
Maybe he should put the speakers
 on the inside of his car.

1186
00:47:16,010 --> 00:47:20,590
-Hey, threw meat
 loaf at my mom today.

1187
00:47:20,590 --> 00:47:24,180
-I'm going to be involved
 with a Sagittarius this week.

1188
00:47:24,180 --> 00:47:28,620
-Two teens overdose
 on angel dust?

1189
00:47:28,620 --> 00:47:30,580
-What is up with Mark Trail?

1190
00:47:30,580 --> 00:47:32,400
-Peter never did any dust, man.

1191
00:47:32,400 --> 00:47:34,350
-He was a crack head.

1192
00:47:34,350 --> 00:47:35,730
-What's going on?

1193
00:47:35,730 --> 00:47:36,620
-Are they really dead?

1194
00:47:36,620 --> 00:47:37,680
I--I don't believe it's them.

1195
00:47:37,680 --> 00:47:38,580
There must be some mistake.

1196
00:47:38,580 --> 00:47:41,950
-Yeah. yes, they're really dead.

1197
00:47:41,950 --> 00:47:44,820
-Where's our order?

1198
00:47:44,820 --> 00:47:46,570
-Man, what is so funny?

1199
00:47:46,570 --> 00:47:49,010
-Did you see Russell
 Baker's column this morning?

1200
00:47:49,010 --> 00:47:50,700
-It's great, man.

1201
00:47:50,700 --> 00:47:51,950
He killed them.

1202
00:47:51,950 --> 00:47:53,790
-What are you talking about?

1203
00:47:53,790 --> 00:47:56,710
-That big goon we
 flattened the other night.

1204
00:47:56,710 --> 00:47:58,700
I guess we didn't finish
 the job after all.

1205
00:47:58,700 --> 00:47:59,410
-Oh, my God.

1206
00:47:59,410 --> 00:48:01,680
-Suddenly the Twist and Creme
 seemed a much darker place.

1207
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:02,930
-Psycho might be right.

1208
00:48:02,930 --> 00:48:05,170
-I thought you said
 no one knew it was us.

1209
00:48:05,170 --> 00:48:07,530
I thought you said
 that no one saw us.

1210
00:48:07,530 --> 00:48:08,030
-Calm down.

1211
00:48:08,030 --> 00:48:09,940
-I'm sorry I was thinking again.

1212
00:48:09,940 --> 00:48:11,380
-Just go in the car, all right?

1213
00:48:11,380 --> 00:48:13,270
I'll be with you in a minute.

1214
00:48:13,270 --> 00:48:13,770
-Go to the car.

1215
00:48:13,770 --> 00:48:17,600
Bring your Dilly Bar
 to the car, honey.

1216
00:48:17,600 --> 00:48:19,290
-I should have
 joined the PGA tour.

1217
00:48:19,290 --> 00:48:22,370
-She's a tough broad, man.

1218
00:48:22,370 --> 00:48:23,420
-Forget her.

1219
00:48:23,420 --> 00:48:25,670
What are we going to do
 about our big friend?

1220
00:48:25,670 --> 00:48:27,840
-Or friends, man.

1221
00:48:27,840 --> 00:48:29,090
I say let 'em come.

1222
00:48:29,090 --> 00:48:30,510
-I'll throw pasta at 'em.

1223
00:48:30,510 --> 00:48:32,500
-I, uh, just might
 scalp me a few.

1224
00:48:32,500 --> 00:48:34,970
-Christ, man, put
 that thing away.

1225
00:48:34,970 --> 00:48:37,550
Someone killed Peter and Susie.

1226
00:48:37,550 --> 00:48:38,840
This isn't a game.

1227
00:48:38,840 --> 00:48:40,350
-Lay off me, man.

1228
00:48:40,350 --> 00:48:41,910
-I just want you to chill out.

1229
00:48:41,910 --> 00:48:44,280
-No way.

1230
00:48:44,280 --> 00:48:45,210
-Why, Jimbo?

1231
00:48:45,210 --> 00:48:48,810
-I'm Generation X, that's why.

1232
00:48:48,810 --> 00:48:51,330
-Because I'm having a good time.

1233
00:48:51,330 --> 00:48:52,970
-Can't you just support
 me in that film?

1234
00:48:58,370 --> 00:49:00,250
-He should try a
 more direct approach.

1235
00:49:00,250 --> 00:49:01,560
-Hands off me, dirt bag!

1236
00:49:01,560 --> 00:49:04,280
-Come on, Mags, won't
 you give me a try.

1237
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:05,790
-I'd never touch you, Terry.

1238
00:49:05,790 --> 00:49:06,760
You're dirt.

1239
00:49:06,760 --> 00:49:08,720
-I'm 21.

1240
00:49:08,720 --> 00:49:11,390
-17 is more like it, right?

1241
00:49:11,390 --> 00:49:12,400
-17 and a half.

1242
00:49:12,400 --> 00:49:16,300
-Look, you may be tough,
 but I don't rob the cradle.

1243
00:49:16,300 --> 00:49:18,550
I'm old enough to be
 your older sister.

1244
00:49:18,550 --> 00:49:20,570
-Besides, I've got a career.

1245
00:49:20,570 --> 00:49:22,430
-I like that.

1246
00:49:22,430 --> 00:49:24,580
I've always wanted to make
 it with my older sister.

1247
00:49:24,580 --> 00:49:28,630
-Oh, so Canada has a South, too.

1248
00:49:28,630 --> 00:49:30,250
-I don't want to see you.

1249
00:49:30,250 --> 00:49:31,460
-OK, Friday then?

1250
00:49:31,460 --> 00:49:33,750
-Yeah, well, uh,
 you're not going

1251
00:49:33,750 --> 00:49:36,300
to do any better
 in this town, baby.

1252
00:49:36,300 --> 00:49:37,230
-No town is that small.

1253
00:49:37,230 --> 00:49:40,920
-I'm really sorry,
 but my religion

1254
00:49:40,920 --> 00:49:42,770
forbids inter-species mating.

1255
00:49:42,770 --> 00:49:45,180
-So she's, uh, not a Unitarian?

1256
00:49:45,180 --> 00:49:46,770
-You're smart, aren't you?

1257
00:49:46,770 --> 00:49:50,030
But you'll have it,
 and you will love it.

1258
00:49:50,030 --> 00:49:51,160
-Heh.

1259
00:49:51,160 --> 00:49:53,160
-No, he hasn't really
 sold himself on that one.

1260
00:49:53,160 --> 00:49:53,660
-No.

1261
00:49:53,660 --> 00:49:55,000
-What are you looking at?

1262
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:56,800
Eat your ice cream!

1263
00:49:56,800 --> 00:50:00,260
-I'm going to Dairy
 Queen from now on.

1264
00:50:00,260 --> 00:50:02,420
-The police station--
 the hot new disco.

1265
00:50:04,840 --> 00:50:05,340
[KNOCKING]

1266
00:50:05,340 --> 00:50:07,280
-What's this?

1267
00:50:07,280 --> 00:50:09,210
-Come in.

1268
00:50:09,210 --> 00:50:11,790
-Doogie Howser, detective.

1269
00:50:11,790 --> 00:50:15,470
-[HUMS]

1270
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:18,180
-This is the report
 on our double suicide.

1271
00:50:18,180 --> 00:50:19,240
-And my bibliography, too.

1272
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:22,260
-The coroner fixes the
 death at about 12:30 AM.

1273
00:50:22,260 --> 00:50:24,680
Brain death caused by
 the cervical vertebrae

1274
00:50:24,680 --> 00:50:26,150
being crushed.

1275
00:50:26,150 --> 00:50:26,650
-I guess.

1276
00:50:26,650 --> 00:50:29,070
-Forensics found lots of prints
 on the scene, but few of them

1277
00:50:29,070 --> 00:50:30,720
are clear enough to trace.

1278
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:32,740
The few fingerprints
 we did get all,

1279
00:50:32,740 --> 00:50:34,800
uh, trace back to
 members of the academy--

1280
00:50:34,800 --> 00:50:35,760
-Whom I'd like to thank.

1281
00:50:35,760 --> 00:50:36,850
---employees.

1282
00:50:36,850 --> 00:50:38,000
We've had men checking them out.

1283
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:39,600
They all seem to have
 pretty good alibis

1284
00:50:39,600 --> 00:50:42,100
as to where they
 were last night.

1285
00:50:42,100 --> 00:50:43,960
And I checked with
 mental health to see

1286
00:50:43,960 --> 00:50:46,500
if they had any sizable
 lunatics running around,

1287
00:50:46,500 --> 00:50:50,580
but, uh, they didn't have any
 loose nuts to fit our needs.

1288
00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:52,730
-Hmm?

1289
00:50:52,730 --> 00:50:55,210
-Are you telling me in
 your quaint way, Frank,

1290
00:50:55,210 --> 00:50:57,000
that we don't have any leads?

1291
00:50:57,000 --> 00:50:58,760
-Uh.

1292
00:50:58,760 --> 00:51:00,450
-Why do you hate me, sir?

1293
00:51:00,450 --> 00:51:03,360
-Cap, where did the
 newspapers get the, uh,

1294
00:51:03,360 --> 00:51:05,980
drug and suicide story?

1295
00:51:05,980 --> 00:51:07,500
-I gave it to them.

1296
00:51:07,500 --> 00:51:08,610
-You gave it to them?

1297
00:51:08,610 --> 00:51:09,800
I don't understand.

1298
00:51:09,800 --> 00:51:10,300
-I was bored.

1299
00:51:10,300 --> 00:51:10,880
What do you want?

1300
00:51:10,880 --> 00:51:13,760
-Frank, this Winster boy
 ran with the bad crowd--

1301
00:51:13,760 --> 00:51:14,980
high school kids--

1302
00:51:14,980 --> 00:51:16,240
-No!

1303
00:51:16,240 --> 00:51:17,790
---running red lights,
 getting drunk--

1304
00:51:17,790 --> 00:51:18,290
-Wow.

1305
00:51:18,290 --> 00:51:23,000
---smoking marijuana,
 all the usual bad stuff.

1306
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:25,220
Murder's a whole new ballgame.

1307
00:51:25,220 --> 00:51:26,830
Till we get a line
 on this killer,

1308
00:51:26,830 --> 00:51:29,650
I want the press to get
 nothing but misinformation.

1309
00:51:29,650 --> 00:51:31,170
-So, business as usual?

1310
00:51:31,170 --> 00:51:34,430
-Otherwise they'll make
 this guy a serial killer

1311
00:51:34,430 --> 00:51:36,520
or a goddamn vigilante savior.

1312
00:51:36,520 --> 00:51:37,020
-Hey.

1313
00:51:39,810 --> 00:51:42,010
-What about the
 public's right to know?

1314
00:51:42,010 --> 00:51:45,490
-Hey, we're concerned with
 the public's right to love.

1315
00:51:45,490 --> 00:51:47,030
I've spoken with the parents.

1316
00:51:47,030 --> 00:51:49,490
They've told me they're
 going to cooperate.

1317
00:51:49,490 --> 00:51:52,100
The last thing I want
 is for this kid's gang

1318
00:51:52,100 --> 00:51:54,350
to go looking for revenge.

1319
00:51:54,350 --> 00:51:56,310
-Yeah.

1320
00:51:56,310 --> 00:51:58,850
Well, whatever you say, Cap.

